    {
      "chunk": {
        "id": "10a57a19c6a746b9",
        "text": "Token counts in this note come from the heuristic counter, not a model tokenizer.\n\nFixed windows\n\nThe simplest strategy cuts the text every N tokens with an overlap of M tokens. It is predictable and cheap, and every chunk has the same cost to embed. It is also blind to structure: a window will happily start in the middle of a table row or end halfway through a definition.",
        "embed_text": null,
