    {
      "chunk": {
        "id": "df092ff8a937983e",
        "text": "Why chunk boundaries matter\n\nA retriever never sees a document. It sees chunks, and it can only return what a chunk contains. If the sentence that answers a question is split across two chunks, neither half may score well enough to be retrieved, and the generator is left to guess. Boundary placement is therefore a recall decision disguised as a preprocessing step.",
        "embed_text": null,
        "start_char": 0,
        "end_char": 366,
        "token_count": 69,
